<ul>
<li><p><strong>Precision:</strong> Indicates the percentage of true positive predictions out of all positive predictions made by the model. It's important when false positives are critical (e.g., fraud detection).</p>
</li>
<li><p><strong>Recall:</strong> Indicates the percentage of true positive predictions out of all actual positives in the data. It's critical when missing a positive instance is costly (e.g., medical diagnoses).</p>
</li>
<li><p><strong>F1 Score:</strong> The harmonic mean of Precision and Recall, providing a balanced metric when there’s an imbalance between Precision and Recall.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
